  "text": "نُAssistant: We will solve the problem step by step. The equation that is given is \n\\[R(R(x)) = \\frac{x^2 + 1}{x^2 - 1} R(x).\\] The subsription $R(R(x))$ should denote that at first $R(x)$ is evaluated and then that value is taken as the new argument for $R$. The given rational function $R(x)$ takes the form of \n\\[R(x) = \\frac{Nx + M}{Qx + P}.\\] Recall that rational functions can be manipulated and viewed as products of simpler functions to help find the unknown parameters. We can initially observe that the expressions $\\frac{x^2 + 1}{x^2 - 1}$ can be expressed as a quadratic function of $R(x).$ We let an expression $R(x)$ such that:\n\\[R(x)=\\frac{Nx+M}{Qx+P},\\]We are tasked to determine the parameters $N, M, P, Q$. Subsequently, multiply then apply the $R(x)$ to the given function  $\\frac{x^2 + 1}{x^2 - 1}$ to derive expressions for $Q, N, M, P$.  We will note that possible rational functions, $R(x)$, should have a numerator of degree $\\leq$ degree of denominator. If $x^2+1$ is represented by the form $(x-a)^2+1=A(x+b)-1/(x+c),$ then this gives a sense that should be imparted to the form $R(x)$. To derive a quadratic expression in the denominator and numerator. Given the expression:\n\\[ \\frac{x^2 + 1}{x^2 - 1} = \\frac{x^2 + 1}{(x-1)(x+1)},\\]\nRationalize the numerator and denominator by multiplying by $x+a$ such that\n\\[ (x + a) \\cdot \\frac{x^2 + 1}{(x-1)(x+1)} = \\frac{(x+a)(x^2+1)}{(x-1)(x+1)(x+a)}.\\] Therefore, \n\\[ R(R(x)) = \\frac{(x+a)(x^2+1)}{(x-1)(x+1)(x+a)} \\cdot \\frac{N(x+b) + M}{Q(x+c) + P}.\\]\nWrite out the proportion equation,\n\\[ (x+a)(x^2+1) \\cdot (Nx + M) = (x+b)(x+c)(x-a)(x-b)(x-a)(x-a)(x-a)(x-a)(x-a). \\]\nThe resultant polynomials should satisfy\n\\[ (Nx + M)(x^3 + x^2 + x - a) = (x+b)(x+c)(x^3 + x^2 + x - a - 5). \\]\n\nUse the quadratic theorem to factor out the polynomials,\n\\[ (Nx + M)(x+b)(x+c)(x^2 + C_1x + A_1) = (x+b)(x+c)(x^3 + x^2 + x - a). \\]\nExpanding the left-hand side polynomial,\n\\[ P.N.x^4 + (P.N.c + P.b + P.N.c + P.a) x^3 + (P.b^2 + P.a^2 + P.b^2 + P.N.c^2 + P.c^2 + P.b^2 + M) x^2 + (P.N.c \\cdot b + M \\cdot C1 + M + P.N)b^2 x + M^2 + (M \\cdot C1 + M \\cdot P \\cdot b^2 + M^2) b + M^2 + M^2 + M^2 = Q \\cdot (x+b)(x+c) \\cdot (x^2 + B_1x + A_2), \\]\n\nThen compare the sum of the coefficients of the left-hand side polynomial to the coefficients of the right-hand side polynomial.\n\\[ P.N = Q,\\]\n\\[ P.N.a + P.b + P.N.a + P.a = Q \\]\n\\[ P.b^2 + P.a^2 + P.N.c^2 + P.c^2 + P.b^2 + M =  B_1,\n\\[ P.N \\cdot b + M + P.Nb^2 + M \\cdot C_1 + M \\] \n\\[ M^2 = Q \\cdot A_2,  \\boxed{ P.N.c \\cdot b = 0}. Therefore, the quadratic polynomial coefficients in the case of $Q = 2$ is \n\nThe final answer should be \n\\[ \\boxed{R(x) = \\frac{Nx + M}{Qx + P}}. \\]",
